[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is no `[[bin]]`/`main.rs` in either tree, so there is no driver stdout to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m diff.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime option/mode axis (A) — the permission flag bitmask.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `matrixsum` derives `permissions` from the truthiness of its four `int`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m arguments (`lib.c:135-151`) and `process_flags` counts the set bits of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `FLAG_READ|FLAG_WRITE|FLAG_EXECUTE|FLAG_DELETE` nibble (`lib.c:94-113`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m That is a 4-bit option space: **16 distinct modes**, each taking a different
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m combination of the four `if`s.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime state axis (B) — the mutable `matrix` global.**
